<div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
  <%= t("privacy_zones.panel") %>
</div>

<h2>What a zone is</h2>
<p>
  A circle you draw around a place you do not want to reveal — your home, your
  workplace, a relative's house. You create them in
  <%= link_to "Privacy zones", privacy_zones_path %>, by searching a place or
  clicking the map, and choose the radius. The zones themselves are never
  shared.
</p>

<h2>What it hides</h2>
<p>
  When you publish, every point of the route inside one of your zones is cut out
  before the copy is made: from the route on the map, the map image, the GPX
  file, and the positions of photos. The route is drawn with a gap there, so
  nobody can follow it to the door.
</p>

<h2>The start and the finish</h2>
<p>
  The start and the finish are where a route gives a place away most easily,
  so each publishing profile decides about them separately, with
  <strong>mask the start</strong> and <strong>mask the finish</strong>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Mask checked</strong> — the start (or the finish) must lie inside
    one of your zones, and is removed with it. If no zone covers it, Allure
    refuses to publish and tells you why, rather than reveal it.</li>
  <li><strong>Mask unchecked</strong> — the start (or the finish) stays visible,
    <strong>even inside a zone</strong>. Use it for routes that start somewhere
    public, like a trailhead or a club.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  If a part of the recording never leaves a zone, there is nothing left to show
  safely, and the route is not published.
</p>

<h2>What it never changes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Your own workout: you still see the whole route, and your figures are
    computed from it.</li>
  <li>Publications already made: they are copies, frozen when you published.
    Adding a zone later does not reach them — delete them and publish again.</li>
  <li>Deleting a zone does not reveal anything already published, but your next
    publications will no longer hide that area.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Photos and segments</h2>
<ul>
  <li>A photo taken inside a zone is left out of a publication unless you
    explicitly include it, and is then shared without its position.</li>
  <li>Your efforts on a segment that one of your zones touches never appear on
    its leaderboard.</li>
  <li>Sharing a course of your own that crosses a zone asks for your
    confirmation first.</li>
</ul>
